ers/indiebuildinganton-gif","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indiebuildinganton-gif/pleeno-monorepo/commits/37f3cf72e02f309554877f44782c5a6c58b008a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-12-17T05:49:40Z","email":"indiebuildinganton@gmail.com","name":"mystbrent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-12-17T05:49:40Z","email":"indiebuildinganton@gmail.com","name":"mystbrent"},"message":"fix: simplify proxy and vercel config for Edge Runtime compatibility\n\nPhase 1 code changes per research findings:\n\n1. Simplified all proxy.ts files to minimal pass-through\n   - Removed async keyword (not needed)\n   - Removed console.log statements\n   - Just return NextResponse.next()\n\n2. Updated all vercel.json files\n   - Removed custom buildCommand (Vercel ignores it in pnpm monorepos - documented bug)\n   - Set framework: ''nextjs'' for auto-detection\n   - Let Vercel handle workspace dependency resolution\n\nWhy: Research identified 3 root causes:\n- middleware.ts deprecated in Next.js 16 (already using proxy.ts)\n- Vercel ignores custom buildCommand in pnpm workspaces\n- Edge Runtime has strict bundling requirements\n\nTesting: Minimal proxy to verify Edge Runtime initialization works\nNext: Configure Vercel dashboard (Root Directory + Environment Variables)\n\nRelated: docs/deployment/fix-vercel-500-error/deep_research.md","tree":{"sha":"5a3e9d8deee5ce0ff922040837b8a625d877ba18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indiebuildinganton-gif/pleeno-monorepo/git/trees/5a3e9d8deee5ce0ff922040837b8a625d877ba18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indiebuildinganton-gif/pleeno-monorepo/git/commits/37f3cf72e02f309554877f44782c5a6c58b008a3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234336247?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/indiebuildinganton-gif/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https:/